# logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# local deploy-script run state (machine-specific, no secrets, safe to delete).
# The .tmp-<pid> variant is the atomic-write scratch file — it's supposed to
# be transient (write, then rename over the real file), but a Windows-only
# EPERM race (something else briefly holding the destination handle, e.g.
# antivirus) can leave it stranded. Ignore it too so a deploy that hits that
# race doesn't surface as a false "uncommitted change" warning.
/.kv-purge-state.json
/.kv-purge-state.json.tmp-*

# Plugin/skill artifacts dropped into .claude/ by Cowork sessions - never ship, never commit
.claude/*
!.claude/launch.json

# Dated sync-backup copy of the KB reference file -- 28 commits of drift, pure
# safety-copy noise from the nightly auto-sync job. Identified 2026-07-27
# (MASTER-FIX-BLUEPRINT Phase 4). Leaving figures-reference-v2.js and
# figures-reference-v2.slim.js tracked -- both look like real build inputs,
# not backups; not touching those without confirming the build actually needs them.
src/data/figures-reference-v2.js.backup-pre-sync
